 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "18:1-4 «إنما يعمر مساجد الله» is not glossed (any cut of Al-Muyassar's «لا يعتني… إلا» would split the restriction). No mosque building drawn: geometric near «مساجد الله», light for the prayer, coins for the zakat, a lamp for «المهتدين». The Fire (17:15-18): text only, nothing drawn. STAGING v4: c1 (17) stays ambient: a negated clause (it is not for the polytheists to maintain the mosques), their deeds void (Al-Muyassar: on the Day of Resurrection) and the Fire; nobody is drawn, no plate stands for the mosques; a wind plate for the deeds made void (17:13), gone before the Fire is named. c2 (18): a prayer hall by day (no Kaaba, no Sacred Mosque, no writing): three believers at the centre stand in prayer on 18:2 (maintaining the mosques; As-Sa'di: by worship and prayer), bow on 18:5 and prostrate on 18:10 (they establish the prayer), facing an empty part of the hall; the camera stays wide on the Name (18:4). They stand up on 18:11; a poor man comes in and sits at the left on 18:12 (after the prayer), and they give him their zakat on 18:13 (As-Sa'di: to those entitled to it); he raises his hands on 18:14; the believers lower their heads on 18:16 (they fear none but Allah). A lamp plate for the rightly guided (18:23). No lone man at the centre, no imam."
